  4	//! whether the predicate held, never a pass), `pass_absolute_range` (the
  5	//! expected value has no binary64 value; separately counted), or
  6	//! `structural_zero` (no published row by construction; R1's value must be
  7	//! exactly 0), or `expected_unresolved` (the row of a case on the committed
  8	//! expected-unresolved list, which ended honestly unresolved with no rows:
  9	//! ROOT's ruling on THIN-A and THIN-B; never a pass). The report shows
 10	//! passes, absolute-range passes and not-covered comparisons as three
 11	//! separate numbers, and the six tallies must add up to the rows compared.
